          "url": "https://www.last.fm/music/Propaganda/A+Secret+Wish",
          "wiki": {
            "content": "\n\"A Secret Wish\" was the 1985 debut album of synthpop band \"Propaganda\". It was produced by Stephen Lipson and Trevor Horn.\n\nThe album shares many of the characteristics of other early-'80s ZTT releases, especially in the groundbreaking use of synthesizers, such as the Fairlight CMI.\n\nThe singles \"Duel\" and \"Dr. Mabuse\" were both successful UK chart hits. The track \"p:Machinery\" was also released as a single, and was featured in an episode of the 80's TV \"Show Miami Vice\".\n <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Propaganda/A+Secret+Wish\">Read more on Last.fm</a>. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.",
            "published": "04 Apr 2009, 20:31",
            "summary": "\"A Secret Wish\" was the 1985 debut album of synthpop band \"Propaganda\". It was produced by Stephen Lipson and Trevor Horn. The album shares many of the characteristics of other early-'80s ZTT releases, especially in the groundbreaking use of synthesizers, such as the Fairlight CMI. The singles \"Duel\" and \"Dr. Mabuse\" were both successful UK chart hits. The track \"p:Machinery\" was also released as a single, and was featured in an episode of the 80's TV \"Show Miami Vice\". <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Propaganda/A+Secret+Wish\">Read more on Last.fm</a>."
          }
        }
